---
/**
 * projects.astro - Projects & Competitions page
 * 
 * ZERO-JS: This page ships no JavaScript - CSS-only animations for badges.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Grant Palasak | Projects" 
  description="Portfolio of security-focused projects including Burp Suite extensions, homelab infrastructure, and UI/UX experiments by Grant Palasak."
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mb-2 font-mono">Projects</h1>
  <p class="text-gray-400 mb-10">A curated selection of work reflecting my focus on security tooling, infrastructure design, and modern development practices.</p>

  <div class="space-y-10">

    <!-- Project Kepler -->
    <div class="project-card bg-gray-800/50 border border-gray-700 rounded-lg p-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-cyan-400 font-mono">projectKepler</h2>
        <span class="status-badge status-active">Active Tooling</span>
        <span class="new-badge">New</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 italic mb-4">Solving documentation debt in collaborative penetration testing.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">Built to facilitate seamless handoffs between testers. projectKepler allows users to tag endpoints as vulnerable, safe, or "needs investigation" directly within Burp Suite's proxy. The goal was to prevent redundant testing and create a shared understanding of what's been covered—a common pain point in team-based engagements.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
        <span class="tech-tag">Java 17</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Burp Extender API</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">JSON Persistence</span>
      </div>
      <a href="https://github.com/gjpalasak42/projectKepler" target="_blank" class="inline-block bg-cyan-900/50 border border-cyan-500 text-cyan-400 font-semibold py-2 px-4 rounded hover:bg-cyan-800/50 transition duration-300 text-sm">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>

    <!-- dockerLab -->
    <div class="project-card bg-gray-800/50 border border-gray-700 rounded-lg p-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-cyan-400 font-mono">dockerLab</h2>
        <span class="status-badge status-live">Live Infrastructure</span>
        <span class="new-badge">New</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 italic mb-4">Security-first homelab orchestration.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">This stack currently hosts the very website you're reading. It's a production-ready environment running on local hardware, utilizing Astro for zero-JS static generation and Bun for blazing-fast builds. Cloudflare Tunnels provide zero-trust, localhost-only exposure. The architecture prioritizes minimal attack surface—there are no publicly exposed ports, and all traffic is authenticated through Cloudflare's network.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
        <span class="tech-tag">Docker</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Astro</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Bun</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Tailwind CSS</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Cloudflare Zero Trust</span>
      </div>
      <a href="https://github.com/gjpalasak42/dockerLab" target="_blank" class="inline-block bg-cyan-900/50 border border-cyan-500 text-cyan-400 font-semibold py-2 px-4 rounded hover:bg-cyan-800/50 transition duration-300 text-sm">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>

    <!-- threat-tracker -->
    <div class="project-card bg-gray-800/50 border border-gray-700 rounded-lg p-6">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-cyan-400 font-mono">threat-tracker</h2>
        <span class="status-badge status-experiment">UI/UX Experiment</span>
        <span class="new-badge">New</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 italic mb-4">A UI/UX experiment in threat intelligence visualization.</p>
      <p class="mb-4">A proof-of-concept platform built to explore Next.js 16 and Tailwind CSS 4. While it functions as a simple OSINT lookup tool for AbuseIPDB and AlienVault OTX, its primary purpose was an exploration of modern frontend architecture—specifically, real-time data streaming with Server-Sent Events (SSE) and schema management with Drizzle ORM.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
        <span class="tech-tag">Next.js 16</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">TypeScript</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Drizzle ORM</span>
        <span class="tech-tag">Tailwind CSS 4</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a href="https://github.com/gjpalasak42/threat-tracker" target="_blank" class="inline-block bg-cyan-900/50 border border-cyan-500 text-cyan-400 font-semibold py-2 px-4 rounded hover:bg-cyan-800/50 transition duration-300 text-sm">View on GitHub</a>
          <a href="https://intel.palasak.com" target="_blank" class="inline-block bg-cyan-900/50 border border-cyan-500 text-cyan-400 font-semibold py-2 px-4 rounded hover:bg-cyan-800/50 transition duration-300 text-sm">View Live</a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 italic">Note: You can create your own account to use the system today!</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Certifications -->
    <div class="project-card bg-gray-800/50 border border-gray-700 rounded-lg p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-cyan-400 mb-2 font-mono">Certifications</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-4">Professional certifications currently in progress.</p>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        <div class="bg-gray-900/50 rounded p-3">
          <p class="font-bold text-white">Hack The Box - Certified Penetration Testing Specialist (CPTS)</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-yellow-400">In Progress</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-900/50 rounded p-3">
          <p class="font-bold text-white">TCM Security - Practical Network Penetration Tester (PNPT)</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-yellow-400">In Progress</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CPTC -->
    <div class="project-card bg-gray-800/50 border border-gray-700 rounded-lg p-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-cyan-400 mb-2 font-mono">Collegiate Penetration Testing Competition (CPTC)</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-4">Former Team Captain for Tennessee Tech's CyberEagles</p>
      <p class="mb-4">As team captain, I led strategy, technical execution, and client-facing presentations in a simulated, real-world penetration testing engagement against live enterprise networks. This competition was a premier event for developing and demonstrating practical offensive security skills.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-center">
        <div class="bg-gray-900/50 rounded p-3">
          <p class="font-bold text-white">CPTC 10 (2024)</p>
          <p class="text-lg text-green-400">1st Place - Central Region</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-gray-900/50 rounded p-3">
          <p class="font-bold text-white">CPTC 11 (2025)</p>
          <p class="text-lg text-cyan-400">3rd Place - Central Region</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- Workflow Section -->
  <section class="mt-16 pt-8 border-t border-gray-700/50">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-4 font-mono">// Development Workflow</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      These projects were developed using an agentic workflow with tools like Google's Antigravity and GitHub Copilot. My interest lies in exploring how AI can meaningfully augment security hardening, automate repetitive code review, and accelerate CI/CD pipelines—while keeping the human in the loop for critical decisions. This approach reflects my belief that effective security work is about amplifying expertise, not replacing it.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
